@pyq U.P. Lower Sub. (Spl.) (Pre) 2002
Consider the following statements in context to Agni (II) missile which was launched in space on January 25, 2002.
1. It is a surface-to-surface missile with a range of 700 km.
2. It was launched at 8:45 am in space from Wheeler's Island, Orissa.
3. It is a two-stage missile whose first phase has a liquid propellant rocket motor and in second, has a solid propellant rocket motor.
(a) Only 1
(b) 1 and 2
(c) 2 and 3
(d) 1 and 3
@ans (*)
@note The missile fired on **25 January 2002** was the new short-range **Agni-I** (about 700 km, single-stage **solid** fuel), not Agni-II, and Agni-II's two stages are both solid. The mixed-up statements leave no clean answer, so the source marks it (*).
@end
