**Operation Pawan** (1987) was the IPKF operation against the LTTE in **Jaffna**, Sri Lanka. Other named operations: **Vijay** (Goa 1961; Kargil 1999), **Meghdoot** (Siachen, 1984), **Blue Star** (1984), **Shakti** (Pokhran-II, 1998), **Ganga** (evacuation from Ukraine, 2022), **Kaveri** (Sudan, 2023), **Ajay** (Israel, 2023) and **Sindoor** (May 2025).

@trap
**Prithvi = surface-to-surface, Trishul and Akash = surface-to-air, Nag = anti-tank, Astra = air-to-air, Rudram = air-to-surface.** **BrahMos = India + Russia**, supersonic; **Nirbhay is subsonic**. **Iron Dome, Phalcon and Barak = Israel.** **Tejas** is a fighter, **Hansa** a trainer. **INS Vikramaditya = ex-Admiral Gorshkov.** **Khanjar = Kyrgyzstan.** Agni-II is **not** an ICBM.
@end

@heatmap

@pattern
Defence questions have two layers: a **permanent** layer of missile types and partners (Prithvi, Agni, Nag, BrahMos, Israel's systems) asked since the 1990s, and a **current** layer of tests, deliveries and exercises from the year before the exam (2023-2025: Vagir, Rudram-II, FWD-200B, BrahMos to the Philippines, Khanjar-XII, Iron Dome).
@end

@next
Likely next angles: **Operation Sindoor** and the systems used (S-400, Akash, BrahMos, loitering munitions), **Agni-V MIRV**, the **long-range hypersonic missile** (November 2024), **INS Arighaat**, the **Tejas Mk1A** and **AMCA** stealth fighter, **Project Kusha** air defence, **Sudarshan Chakra Mission**, the **Defence Industrial Corridors** of UP and Tamil Nadu, and defence exports.
@end
